    "a": "The screen comparisons (M72) and the prohibition-against-no-channel comparisons (M67, M68) use the two-sided permutation test registered in amendments 5 and 4 (b): p is the share of relabellings of the pool sessions with |statistic| at least the observed one. With 4 against 4 pool sessions and complete separation, the observed relabelling and its mirror image both reach it: p = 2/70 = 0.029. With 8 against 4 pool sessions (fine_screen against the 8-pool fine sample) the groups differ in size, so no mirror relabelling exists and only the observed one reaches it: p = 1/495 = 0.002, the same as the one-sided minimum. The scorecard rows (M64) are one-sided in the humans' direction (amendment 4 (a)): minimum 1/70 = 0.014 for 4 against 4. No add-one correction is applied to exact tests.",
